<title>SWEDEN: Norrporten buys property from Skanska, Skandia.</title>
<headline>Norrporten buys property from Skanska, Skandia.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish property group Norrporten said on Tuesday it had bought 21 properties in northern Sweden from insurer Skandia and construction group Skanska for 717 million crowns.  </p>
<p>Norrporten said in a statement that 501 million crowns would be paid in cash and 216 million through a new share issue.</p>
<p>After the acquisitions Norrporten's property book value will be 2.17 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The company said the deal was subject to approval from the Finance Inspectorate.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
